ut we like them together so  we aren't too upset about it all of the  scenes with Maddy are different from the  way things went in the books even though  we like some of the changes that they  made before bringing the characters to  life it's kind of strange to see the  storylines veer especially if you are a  super fan like we are we thought we  would know how everything would turn out  after reading the books but that is not  the case at all how do the changes in  the scenes make you feel are you  screaming at the television or are you  happy with the changes make sure to let  us know your feelings in the comments  Clary okay so we know that Clary is the  main character and everything but did  you like her in the books a lot of  readers had issues with her because of  how she acted towards other female  characters in the books she doesn't  really get along with Izzy and that  would normally be fine but it seems like  the reason they didn't get along was  that Clary was jealous in the TV show  their relationship is quite different  the two seem to be friends from the  start Clary is also a lot closer to her  mom on the show than she was in the  books as well it could be due to the  fact that TV query is older than book  Clary and probably appreciates her mom a  bit more than book Clary  in the show Clary also has a lot more  going for her than in the books at the  beginning of the show she's accepted  into an advanced program at the Brooklyn  Academy of Art talked about ambition  again this difference possibly occurs  due to her age at 15 it probably would  be a little hard for Clary to be  accepted into such a prestigious program  which do you like better  the book version of Clary or the TV  Clary Simon poor Simon he showed up a  lot more in the books than he did on the  TV show in the books he was a geeky  mortal for quite a while it wasn't until  the second book that he transformed into  a vampire and was sired by Rafael so we  got to know his character a lot better  on the television show he was  transformed in the first season and it  wasn't even at the end of the season  either it was in episode three on the  show Camille who was a vampire let's  time invite her while they were making  out a lot of people who were fans of the  books were super mad about this  diversion why because having Simon  changed so early meant that so many  other things in the books would have to  change so much will have to be cut out  because Simon is already a vampire so if  you were looking forward to seeing any  of Simon's non-vampire moments on screen  then you are not  to be a happy camper but this does mean  that we are going to get to see a lot  more of vampire Simon than we did in the  books and who knows maybe people like it  this way better jobs watching the  Shadowhunter show is like playing a game  of Clue to figure out what they changed  from the books and what they added in if  you read the books and now watch the  show you will notice that there is a  huge difference in the jobs of a lot of  the characters in the books  Clary's mom Jocelyn is an artist but you  may have forgotten this because in the  show she owns an antique store they may  have done this because they wanted  Clary's mom to look like she had a more  stable job but we are not 100% certain  why this change occurred as we mentioned  before lugar Way owns a bookstore in the  books which made sense because it  matched his sword of meek personality  but in the show he is an officer with  the NYPD  this wouldn't have made sense in the  books but somehow on the show it makes  perfect sense another weird thing is  that on the show Simon is an accounting  student which isn't exactly a profession  but in the books he is a high school  student we wonder what the reason for  all these switches was where the  television writers just bored and  wanting to shake things up a bit  glamouring okay so changing ages and  small things about characters makes  sense sometimes after all the show could  be half as sultry as it is if all the  characters were actually sixteen on the  show that would just be creepy but when  the writers change a whole storyline  that's when it can get a bit too much  one time that occurred was in episode 10  of the television show when the truth  about Michael Wayland was exposed Jase  recognized him as his father immediately  this was because Valentine had glamoured  himself to look like Michael but in the  books this hold reveal went a bit  differently in the written series  Valentine didn't change his appearance  to look like Michael he only took on  Michael's name and identity which caused  Jase not to instantly recognize him  maybe they were running out of time on  the show and it needed to speed up the  process or maybe it's a bit harder to  show things that are described in books  whereas in the book they could describe  how Jay slowly began to recognize  Michael but in the show that's a little  bit harder to portray this version was  probably much easier for an audience to  digest Jase and Valentine's relationship  every relationship is different from  chips to romantic relationships it all  comes down to how both people feel about  one another some relationships on the  show are quite different from the ones  in the books which relationship are we  talking about in particular the one  between Jace and Valentine in the books  Jace thinks about teaming up with  Valentine and working with him although  he thinks about it he never really  voices these intentions he also never  actually does team up with Valentine on  the television show that is not the case  at the end of season 1 Jace does decide  to team up with Valentine granted there  was some coercion involved with that  decision but at the end of the day Jace  does work with Valentine which makes us  wonder how this will cause the future of  the show to differ from the book it's  kind of like a chain of events one  change causes 1,000 others will this  difference completely change the way  that Jace is feature goes on the show it  definitely has the potential to cause  some big waves such a big partnership  cannot happen without repercussions we  guess we will have to stay tuned to find  out how everything shakes out in the end  the mortal cup if you were just watching  Shadowhunters and hadn't read the books  you might not have any problems with the  storyline but for those of us who are  diehard fans of the books we have more  than a few issues one for instance is  the fact that the mortal cup has a  completely different use in a series  than it did in the books granted the  mortal cup is pretty important in both  versions on the show they say that if a  human has a drink from the cup they will  die which is really strange because in  the book if a human drinks from the cup  they will transform into a Shadowhunter  it also is a lot more valuable in the  show than it was in the books in the  show lots of Downworlders want the cup  but in the book only a few people wanted  it another thing that was different on  the show was the number of times that  Clary used to the cup in the book Clary  never used the cup to control any demons  on the TV show she does it quite often  Clary use of the cop does make the show  a bit more interesting to watch so we  can see why the show's creators would  change the script like that Jocelyn so  in the show  Jocelyn gave Clary a steal at the  beginning of the show which was strange  because the books  Jocelyn would have never done that  Jocelyn didn't want Clary to know  anything about the shadow world  so her giving Clary the steel makes no  sense whatsoever  always super careful to make sure that  Clary wasn't exposed to anything  supernatural in fact she was so  concerned with Clary never finding out  about the magical elements of the world  that she went to Magnus to have him get  rid of Cleary's memories so that she  wouldn't remember anything about the  shadow world  so her giving her the steel actually  goes against everything she has done in  the past this show also had Jocelyn  passed away for some reason in the books  Jocelyn ever passed away so it was weird  when the show would make up such a huge  thing and it didn't even really matter  to the storyline it's like the writers  just got bored and we're like who can we  get rid of today and for some reason  that person was Jocelyn lots of fans of  the books had a big problem with the way  the show handled Jocelyn but the  creators of the show must have had a  reason for doing it more about the  characters okay we don't know about you  but when we write the books we'd like to  pay close attention to the details  especially when the author is describing  the characters it's the first time you  get a feel for who the characters are  and it's the only time you get to create  images of them in your head when the  show creators read through the books  they must have not paid too close  attention to the details of the  characters or maybe they didn't read the  books at all if they would have they  would have known that rad nor fell was  supposed to be green in the show he's  not green at all but just a regular  human tone in the books Katerina is  supposed to be blue if you've watched  the show then you know that that isn't  the case on Shadowhunters  of course these are minor changes that  don't really affect the storyline at all  but it's still annoying wouldn't have  made such a difference if the show's  creators had stuck to the storyline no  it wouldn't have it just would have made  fans of the book a lot more happy right  do you hear that producers it's not too  late your fans will thank you  and that's it for 10 differences between  Shadowhunters books and TV show did we  miss any of the differences let us know  in the comments and don't forget to  check out our sister channel Screen Rant  thanks for watching

